<h2 id=3D"graph-types">Graph Types</h2>
<p><code>pydantic-graph</code> made up of a few key components:</p>
<h3 id=3D"graphruncontext">GraphRunContext</h3>
<p><a class=3D"autorefs autorefs-internal" href=3D"https://ai.pydantic.dev/=
api/pydantic_graph/nodes/#pydantic_graph.nodes.GraphRunContext"><code>Graph=
RunContext</code></a> =E2=80=94 The context for the graph run, similar to P=
ydanticAI's <a class=3D"autorefs autorefs-internal" href=3D"https://ai.pyda=
ntic.dev/api/tools/#pydantic_ai.tools.RunContext"><code>RunContext</code></=
a>. This holds the state of the graph and dependencies and is passed to nod=
es when they're run.</p>
<p><code>GraphRunContext</code> is generic in the state type of the graph i=
t's used in, <a class=3D"autorefs autorefs-internal" href=3D"https://ai.pyd=
antic.dev/api/pydantic_graph/state/#pydantic_graph.state.StateT"><code>Stat=
eT</code></a>.</p>
<h3 id=3D"end">End</h3>
<p><a class=3D"autorefs autorefs-internal" href=3D"https://ai.pydantic.dev/=
api/pydantic_graph/nodes/#pydantic_graph.nodes.End"><code>End</code></a> =
=E2=80=94 return value to indicate the graph run should end.</p>
<p><code>End</code> is generic in the graph return type of the graph it's u=
sed in, <a class=3D"autorefs autorefs-internal" href=3D"https://ai.pydantic=
.dev/api/pydantic_graph/nodes/#pydantic_graph.nodes.RunEndT"><code>RunEndT<=
/code></a>.</p>
<h3 id=3D"nodes">Nodes</h3>
<p>Subclasses of <a class=3D"autorefs autorefs-internal" href=3D"https://ai=
.pydantic.dev/api/pydantic_graph/nodes/#pydantic_graph.nodes.BaseNode"><cod=
e>BaseNode</code></a> define nodes for execution in the graph.</p>
<p>Nodes, which are generally <a class=3D"autorefs autorefs-external" href=
=3D"https://docs.python.org/3/library/dataclasses.html#dataclasses.dataclas=
s"><code>dataclass</code>es</a>, generally consist of:</p>
<ul>
<li>fields containing any parameters required/optional when calling the nod=
e</li>
<li>the business logic to execute the node, in the <a class=3D"autorefs aut=
orefs-internal" href=3D"https://ai.pydantic.dev/api/pydantic_graph/nodes/#p=
ydantic_graph.nodes.BaseNode.run"><code>run</code></a> method</li>
<li>return annotations of the <a class=3D"autorefs autorefs-internal" href=
=3D"https://ai.pydantic.dev/api/pydantic_graph/nodes/#pydantic_graph.nodes.=
BaseNode.run"><code>run</code></a> method, which are read by <code>pydantic=
-graph</code> to determine the outgoing edges of the node</li>
</ul>
<p>Nodes are generic in:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>state</strong>, which must have the same type as the state of g=
raphs they're included in, <a class=3D"autorefs autorefs-internal" href=3D"=
https://ai.pydantic.dev/api/pydantic_graph/state/#pydantic_graph.state.Stat=
eT"><code>StateT</code></a> has a default of <code>None</code>, so if you'r=
e not using state you can omit this generic parameter, see <a data-preview=
=3D"" href=3D"https://ai.pydantic.dev/graph/#stateful-graphs">stateful grap=
hs</a> for more information</li>
<li><strong>deps</strong>, which must have the same type as the deps of the=
 graph they're included in, <a class=3D"autorefs autorefs-internal" href=3D=
"https://ai.pydantic.dev/api/pydantic_graph/nodes/#pydantic_graph.nodes.Dep=
sT"><code>DepsT</code></a> has a default of <code>None</code>, so if you're=
 not using deps you can omit this generic parameter, see <a data-preview=3D=
"" href=3D"https://ai.pydantic.dev/graph/#dependency-injection">dependency =
injection</a> for more information</li>
<li><strong>graph return type</strong> =E2=80=94 this only applies if the n=
ode returns <a class=3D"autorefs autorefs-internal" href=3D"https://ai.pyda=
ntic.dev/api/pydantic_graph/nodes/#pydantic_graph.nodes.End"><code>End</cod=
e></a>. <a class=3D"autorefs autorefs-internal" href=3D"https://ai.pydantic=
.dev/api/pydantic_graph/nodes/#pydantic_graph.nodes.RunEndT"><code>RunEndT<=
/code></a> has a default of <a class=3D"autorefs autorefs-external" href=3D=
"https://docs.python.org/3/library/typing.html#typing.Never">Never</a> so t=
his generic parameter can be omitted if the node doesn't return <code>End</=
code>, but must be included if it does.</li>
</ul>
<p>Here's an example of a start or intermediate node in a graph =E2=80=94 i=
t can't end the run as it doesn't return <a class=3D"autorefs autorefs-inte=
rnal" href=3D"https://ai.pydantic.dev/api/pydantic_graph/nodes/#pydantic_gr=
aph.nodes.End"><code>End</code></a>:</p>
