<p>You maybe have noticed that although this examples transfers control flo=
w out of the graph run, we're still using <a class=3D"autorefs autorefs-ext=
ernal" href=3D"https://rich.readthedocs.io/en/stable/reference/prompt.html#=
rich.prompt.PromptBase.ask">rich's <code>Prompt.ask</code></a> to get user =
input, with the process hanging while we wait for the user to enter a respo=
nse. For an example of genuine out-of-process control flow, see the <a data=
-preview=3D"" href=3D"https://ai.pydantic.dev/examples/question-graph/">que=
stion graph example</a>.</p>
<h2 id=3D"dependency-injection">Dependency Injection</h2>
<p>As with PydanticAI, <code>pydantic-graph</code> supports dependency inje=
ction via a generic parameter on <a class=3D"autorefs autorefs-internal" hr=
ef=3D"https://ai.pydantic.dev/api/pydantic_graph/graph/#pydantic_graph.grap=
h.Graph"><code>Graph</code></a> and <a class=3D"autorefs autorefs-internal"=
 href=3D"https://ai.pydantic.dev/api/pydantic_graph/nodes/#pydantic_graph.n=
odes.BaseNode"><code>BaseNode</code></a>, and the <a class=3D"autorefs auto=
refs-internal" href=3D"https://ai.pydantic.dev/api/pydantic_graph/nodes/#py=
dantic_graph.nodes.GraphRunContext.deps"><code>GraphRunContext.deps</code><=
/a> fields.</p>
