<h2 id=3D"mermaid-diagrams">Mermaid Diagrams</h2>
<p>Pydantic Graph can generate <a href=3D"https://mermaid.js.org/">mermaid<=
/a> <a href=3D"https://mermaid.js.org/syntax/stateDiagram.html"><code>state=
Diagram-v2</code></a> diagrams for graphs, as shown above.</p>
<p>These diagrams can be generated with:</p>
<ul>
<li><a class=3D"autorefs autorefs-internal" href=3D"https://ai.pydantic.dev=
/api/pydantic_graph/graph/#pydantic_graph.graph.Graph.mermaid_code"><code>G=
raph.mermaid_code</code></a> to generate the mermaid code for a graph</li>
<li><a class=3D"autorefs autorefs-internal" href=3D"https://ai.pydantic.dev=
/api/pydantic_graph/graph/#pydantic_graph.graph.Graph.mermaid_image"><code>=
Graph.mermaid_image</code></a> to generate an image of the graph using <a h=
ref=3D"https://mermaid.ink/">mermaid.ink</a></li>
<li><a class=3D"autorefs autorefs-internal" href=3D"https://ai.pydantic.dev=
/api/pydantic_graph/graph/#pydantic_graph.graph.Graph.mermaid_save"><code>G=
raph.mermaid_save</code></a> to generate an image of the graph using <a hre=
f=3D"https://mermaid.ink/">mermaid.ink</a> and save it to a file</li>
</ul>
<p>Beyond the diagrams shown above, you can also customize mermaid diagrams=
 with the following options:</p>
<ul>
<li><a class=3D"autorefs autorefs-internal" href=3D"https://ai.pydantic.dev=
/api/pydantic_graph/nodes/#pydantic_graph.nodes.Edge"><code>Edge</code></a>=
 allows you to apply a label to an edge</li>
<li><a class=3D"autorefs autorefs-internal" href=3D"https://ai.pydantic.dev=
/api/pydantic_graph/nodes/#pydantic_graph.nodes.BaseNode.docstring_notes"><=
code>BaseNode.docstring_notes</code></a> and <a class=3D"autorefs autorefs-=
internal" href=3D"https://ai.pydantic.dev/api/pydantic_graph/nodes/#pydanti=
c_graph.nodes.BaseNode.get_note"><code>BaseNode.get_note</code></a> allows =
you to add notes to nodes</li>
<li>The <a class=3D"autorefs autorefs-internal" href=3D"https://ai.pydantic=
.dev/api/pydantic_graph/graph/#pydantic_graph.graph.Graph.mermaid_code"><co=
de>highlighted_nodes</code></a> parameter allows you to highlight specific =
node(s) in the diagram</li>
</ul>
<p>Putting that together, we can edit the last <a data-preview=3D"" href=3D=
"https://ai.pydantic.dev/graph/#custom-control-flow"><code>ai_q_and_a_graph=
.py</code></a> example to:</p>
<ul>
<li>add labels to some edges</li>
<li>add a note to the <code>Ask</code> node</li>
<li>highlight the <code>Answer</code> node</li>
<li>save the diagram as a <code>PNG</code> image to file</li>
</ul>
